From 9d84a57235f37fa6e7c4c540d49e83f5c7b1cd6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Lee <ethantlee21@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:28:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] apprt: raise an APC that no protocol recognizes as an action,
 so that an embedder can take a private report from a program in the pty

The terminal already captures the payload of an APC that is not Kitty
graphics or the glyph protocol (`apc.Handler.unknown_max_bytes`), but the
stream handler drops it. Nothing in the pty can therefore tell the
embedder anything that a title, a notification or a pwd does not say.

Macterm's zmx fork reports the foreground process of a session to the
attached client as such an APC, so that the tab name, the busy-close
guard and the agent logo of a remote pane follow the host at once, in
the order of the output, in place of a polled ssh probe. APC is the
right carrier: no keyboard produces one, a terminal that does not know
it discards it, and it rides the pane's own connection.

The handler keeps at most `unknown_apc_max_bytes` (4 KiB) of such a
payload and reports it through the surface mailbox as a write request,
the way a pwd change travels. The surface raises `unknown_apc` with the
bytes and the cut flag, and frees the request after the action. The
native apprts take the action as a no-op. The tag is appended last in
both enums, so the existing values do not change.
